---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Security | ZoneOfWar"
  description="How to report a security issue to ZoneOfWar and how we handle vulnerability disclosure."
>
  <Section containerClass="max-w-3xl">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-accent">Trust</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold text-text sm:text-4xl">Security</h1>

    <div class="prose-zow mt-8">
      <p>
        As a cybersecurity company, we hold ourselves to the standard we train others to meet. This page explains how
        to report a security issue in the ZoneOfWar website or platform, separate from our normal marketing contact
        channels.
      </p>

      <h2>Reporting a vulnerability</h2>
      <p>
        If you believe you've found a security vulnerability in ZoneOfWar, email
        <a href="mailto:security@zoneofwar.com">security@zoneofwar.com</a> with a description of the issue, steps to
        reproduce it, and any relevant logs or screenshots. Please do not include real customer data in your report.
      </p>

      <h2>What to expect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Acknowledgement of your report within a reasonable timeframe</li>
        <li>An assessment of severity and impact</li>
        <li>Updates as we work toward a fix</li>
        <li>Credit, if you'd like it, once the issue is resolved</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Responsible disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        We ask that you give us a reasonable opportunity to investigate and address an issue before any public
        disclosure, and that you avoid accessing, modifying or deleting data that isn't yours during your research.
        Testing must stay within the isolated environments provided by ZoneOfWar — see our
        <a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Out of scope</h2>
      <p>
        This channel is for security vulnerabilities only. For general support, sales or partnership questions, use
        our <a href="/contact">Contact page</a> instead.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
